## Lock the rules until the next reboot (-e 2, CIS): nobody, root included, can remove or change a rule of the
## running system; a changed rule set takes effect only through a reboot, which is itself logged. This does not
## get in the way of updates: bootc stages the new image with its /etc (rules included) and the new rules load
## when it boots; a rollback boots the old deployment with its own rules.
## Break-glass (debugging with an extra rule): delete this file and reboot.
-e 2
